                            <h2 class="mb-10">Step-by-Step PMP Exam Preparation Guide</h2>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Success in the PMP exam depends on structured preparation. Below is a practical roadmap to guide your journey — built directly from the methods taught in the Professional Development Unit (PDU) course.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Step 1: Review Eligibility Requirements</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                To apply for the PMP certification, candidates must meet specific PMI requirements:
                            </p>
                            <ul class="list-dotted d-flex flex-column gap-8 mb-10">
                                <li>Bachelor's degree + 36 months of project management experience, OR</li>
                                <li>High school diploma + 60 months of experience, AND</li>
                                <li>35 hours of formal project management education (fulfilled through the PMP Exam Prep Course at PDU).</li>
                            </ul>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Step 2: Enroll in the PDU PMP Exam Prep Course</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Registering for the <a href="https://pdu-edu.org/courses/pmpr-exam-prep-online-course" target="_blank">PMP Exam Prep Course</a> by Professional Development Unit ensures you get a structured study plan, access to mock exams, and direct mentorship from certified instructors.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Step 3: Build a Study Schedule</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Set realistic study goals, commit to consistent daily learning. The PDU course provides detailed study timelines to help students stay on track.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Step 4: Practice with Real Exam Questions</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Our course includes hundreds of <a href="https://pdu-edu.org/courses/pmpr-exam-prep-3-month-online-course" target="_blank">PMP practice tests</a> and simulated exams that mirror the actual exam format. This builds familiarity, improves time management, and helps you identify weak areas.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Step 5: Review and Reinforce Key Concepts</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Revisit critical concepts regularly — process groups, knowledge areas, and project lifecycle management. The PDU learning portal makes this easier with flashcards, downloadable notes, and instructor Q&A sessions.
                            </p>

