                            <h2 class="mb-10">PMP Exam Study Tips for Maximum Success</h2>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Effective exam preparation requires a balance of strategy, consistency, and focus. Here are some expert-backed tips shared by PDU's PMP instructors.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Use the PMBOK® Guide Wisely</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Don't just memorize — understand the relationships between process groups and knowledge areas. The PMBOK® Guide serves as a foundation for the exam.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Leverage Mock Tests</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Regular taking mock exams reduces test anxiety and improves accuracy. Aim for at least three full-length practice exams before your test day.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Join Study Groups</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Collaborating with peers keeps you motivated and exposes you to new perspectives on project management challenges.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Focus on Weak Areas</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                After every mock exam, review your weak areas and revisit those topics using PDU's guided study modules.
                            </p>

                            <h2 class="mb-10">What's Next After Passing the PMP Exam?</h2>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                Achieving your PMP certification is only the beginning. Maintaining it requires continuous learning and professional development.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Earning PDUs (Professional Development Units)</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                To keep your certification active, PMI requires you to earn 60 PDUs every three years. The Professional Development Unit (PDU) offers a variety of continuing education programs and workshops to help you meet this requirement effortlessly.
                            </p>

                            <h3 class="mb-10">Advancing Your Project Management Career</h3>
                            <p class="text-neutral-500 mb-10">
                                With your PMP certification, you can explore advanced roles such as:
                            </p>
